{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation.mirrorSplit_eq_zero_of_equal_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation.mirrorSplit_eq_zero_of_equal_weight","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation.lean#L103-L114","doc":"**Equal proton-set weight kills the split outright.** If the two partners'\nproton sets carry the same total weight — which vertex-transitivity forces only\nwhen they also have equal cardinality, but which can happen accidentally\notherwise — the predicted split is exactly zero, whatever the fluxes.\n\nRecorded because it is the sharpest form of the relocation: the bracket is not\nmerely where the `A`-dependence lives, it is the *only* thing standing between\nthis model and a vanishing prediction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation.mirrorSplit_uniform_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation.mirrorSplit_uniform_eq","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation.lean#L91-L101","doc":"**The uniform case is recovered**, reproducing the merged\n`FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit_eq`: the bracket collapses to\n`a·(|P| − |Q|)`, which on the `d = 1` mirror ladder is just `a`, independent of\nthe nucleus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation.mirrorSplit_nonuniform_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation.mirrorSplit_nonuniform_eq","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation.lean#L73-L89","doc":"**The whole `A`-dependence sits in one bracket.** For any two proton sets the\nsplit factorises, with the total weight `∑ k, a k` cancelling entirely:\n\n  `ΔE = C·m·(φp − φn)·( Σ_{k ∈ P} a k − Σ_{k ∈ Q} a k )`\n\nSo a non-vertex-transitive carrier does not create `A`-dependence; it relocates\nit into a topological quantity of the carrier and the charge assignment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation.fhBoundNonuniform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation.fhBoundNonuniform","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonUniformAcRelocatesTheObligation.lean#L65-L71","doc":"The Freedman–He link-bound functional with a **per-component** weight `a k`\n(dropping vertex-transitivity) and an arbitrary proton set `P`.\n\n`C` absorbs the pure constant `(π/16)^{1/4}`, `m` is `min_k |Flux(X_k)|`, the\ncomponents in `P` carry flux `φp` and those in `Pᶜ` carry `φn`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}